# Part VI — Suggested implementation order

## 24. Build one small working slice at a time

| Milestone | Deliverable | Must pass before continuing |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Inspect repository and confirm setup | App starts locally |
| 2 | Screen + microphone capture | Short recording plays |
| 3 | Pause/resume/stop controls | Recording behavior is consistent |
| 4 | Original file download | Downloaded file plays |
| 5 | Transcript data model and mocked transcript | Word navigation works with test data |
| 6 | Cut schedule and restore behavior | Cuts can be added and restored |
| 7 | Preview skipping | Playback skips cuts without looping |
| 8 | Backend transcription integration | Valid response and failure behavior work |
| 9 | Cut-planner prompt + validator | Invalid AI output is rejected |
| 10 | FFmpeg final rendering | Export is playable and synchronized |
| 11 | Retry and manual-edit fallback | Failure does not destroy the recording |
| 12 | Google sign-in | Authentication works without exposing secrets |
| 13 | Security, privacy, and 30-minute acceptance tests | Required tests pass and limitations are documented |

This is a proposed sequence, not a claim that any milestone is already complete. The exact order may change after inspecting the existing codebase.

