# Part VII — Definition of done

## 25. MVP acceptance checklist

The MVP should not be called ready until the applicable checks below pass:

- [ ] Chrome on Windows can capture the screen and microphone.
- [ ] Start, pause, resume, and stop work as specified.
- [ ] A short original recording can be saved and played.
- [ ] A 30-minute recording is tested, not merely assumed to work.
- [ ] Transcription output is validated before use.
- [ ] Word timestamps stay within the media duration.
- [ ] Clicking transcript words navigates to the expected location.
- [ ] AI cut suggestions follow the schema.
- [ ] Invalid AI cut ranges cannot corrupt playback or export.
- [ ] Users can choose review or automatic mode.
- [ ] Users can restore removed segments.
- [ ] Preview skipping behaves correctly for adjacent and overlapping cuts.
- [ ] AI failures trigger bounded retries and then manual editing.
- [ ] Final export opens in a real media player.
- [ ] Audio/video synchronization is checked.
- [ ] Provider secrets stay server-side.
- [ ] Temporary media handling matches the disclosed retention policy.
- [ ] Tests and known limitations are documented.
- [ ] Unresolved product decisions are explicitly recorded.

A checkbox is complete only after the relevant test has been performed and its result recorded.

---

# Part VIII — Remaining decisions

## 26. Do not silently assume these answers

The following still need explicit decisions:

1. Will ScreenForge be a website, Chrome extension, or both?
2. Which final export format and quality controls will be supported?
3. Can users reopen projects after closing Chrome?
4. Will crash recovery be part of the MVP?
5. What retry count and retry timing should be used?
6. How long can temporary server-side media remain before deletion?
7. What is the default AI cut mode?
8. What resolution and frame rate must be supported?
9. What maximum file size can the backend accept?
10. Which exact Google sign-in and session behaviors are required?

Until these are decided, keep the relevant code modular and make assumptions easy to change.

**End of implementation blueprint.**
